WEBVTT

00:06:59.565 --> 00:07:01.050
There's some dispersal,

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.060
but it's kind of grouped
around that average body type.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.639
Then that idea started to go away,

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:07.340
and at the same time, digital technology --

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.547
first radio, then television and the Internet --

00:07:09.547 --> 00:07:11.924
gave millions, or in some cases billions, of people

00:07:11.924 --> 00:07:15.103
a ticket to consume elite sports performance.

00:07:15.103 --> 00:07:18.976
The financial incentives and fame and glory
afforded elite athletes skyrocketed,

00:07:18.976 --> 00:07:23.169
and it tipped toward the tiny
upper echelon of performance.

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:26.596
It accelerated the artificial
selection for specialized bodies.

00:07:26.596 --> 00:07:28.224
And if you plot a data point for these same

00:07:28.224 --> 00:07:32.106
two dozen sports today, it looks like this.